# Paths the `tauri dev` file watcher must not treat as source changes.
#
# build.rs compiles the Swift menu-bar helper on every build and publishes it
# atomically: build_support/tray_helper.rs stages the binary at
# `helper/.hq-tray-helper.<pid>.tmp`, then renames it over
# `helper/hq-tray-helper`. Both paths sit inside the watched tree, so without
# these entries the watcher sees its own build output land, restarts the
# build, produces a new PID-named temp file, and restarts again — `tauri dev`
# never reaches a running app on macOS. The staging file needs a rule of its
# own; the published-binary rule does not match a dotted, PID-suffixed name.
#
# Keep this narrow. helper/hq-tray-helper.swift and helper/tests are real
# sources and must still trigger a rebuild when edited.
helper/hq-tray-helper
helper/.hq-tray-helper.*.tmp
